      "mergeID": "64cd5e0aace340097db8b4b8",
      "mergedPostDetails": "No known reproduction steps. \n\nKnown affected players approximately 4-5, for several years.\n\nBug description: When joining a world, sometimes other players do not see me, but I see them. I am able to interact with their avatars - for example, grabbing a friend's tail which he has set to freeze his motion upon being grabbed (and he freezes, unable to see me).\n\nThe other player does not see me even in the world player list.\n\nI have to block the player and then unblock him, which makes me appear in the world for him.\n\nThe bug is random. It can happen several times a night, or not at all. *It only happens for specific players*, for example me (Orkel), FunnySwedishGal, Auinakai, Plaster and maybe a couple others. Most players in our social circle never get this bug.\n\nI am not always the \"invisible one\", there are cases where, for example, Auinakai does not see FunnySwedishGal, etc.\n\nThis bug has ruined gameworlds many times. For example a situation where in a tag world, the person being chased does not see the tagger (me) at all. \n\nAnd in social situations, talking a bunch only to realize that the player does not see me.\n\nReinstalling does not fix it. Nothing has fixed it for the past 3 or so years that it has happened for us.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "One person does not see the other. The \"block&unblock\" invisibility bug.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
